# Dashboards complementary to alerts

Do not add or keep an alert without a provisioned Grafana dashboard that
can explain the page. Community imports live in
`collections/ansible_collections/fleet/debian_guest/roles/observability/files/dashboards/`.
Fleet-authored dashboards live in
`collections/ansible_collections/fleet/debian_guest/roles/observability/files/dashboards/fleet/`
(Grafana folder from `foldersFromFilesStructure`). The observability role
copies them onto `proxmox-observability-debian`.

- Prefer a community dashboard (grafana.com / exporter upstream) over a
  hand-rolled one. Import the JSON, then rewrite datasource UIDs to the
  provisioned Prometheus (`http://127.0.0.1:9090` on
  `proxmox-observability-debian`; query from other hosts at
  `http://proxmox-observability-debian:9090`).
- Vet every panel `expr` against live series the same way as alerts
  (`alert-timeseries.mdc`). Fix job/label names (`host` vs `instance`).
  Delete or hide panels whose metrics we do not scrape. Grep `expr`, not
  leftover `"metric"` fields.
- Cover the alert's labels and the surrounding saturation (pool, disk,
  upstream, errors), not a single sparkline.
- List the dashboard on `docs/services/grafana.md` and on the service
  doc. Facts: `docs/services/grafana.md`.
